<!--
    Swift name demangling (`option swiftdemangle on|off`).

    Issue: a Swift binary renders its symbols as mangled soup. On the Toyota
    iOS app (84 MB arm64, Swift + Objective-C) kuna printed the imported
    `$sSo9OS_os_logC0B0E9subsystem8categoryABSS_SStcfC` and, with the ObjC
    metadata pass on, Swift classes under their runtime names
    (`-[_TtC6Toyota24AddMileageViewController viewDidLoad]`). The earlier
    name-only subset demangled 26% of the Swift symbols; the demangler now
    reads the whole stable grammar (`$s`) and the ObjC runtime type names
    (`_Tt`) and demangles all of them.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 environment-binding, the loader's symbol-name
    demangle seam (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/demangle/kuna_swift.rs`,
    reached from `demangle_name` while the symbol table is installed) and the
    ObjC metadata pass's class-name rendering (`analyzers/objc/mod.rs`).

    P0 assertion: `option swiftdemangle on|off` (default on). The gate travels
    as the `KUNA_SWIFTDEMANGLE` environment variable, so it is set before the
    `load file` it must govern.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear
    it and load the real arm64 Mach-O fixture `macho_swift_names_arm64`
    (built from `macho_swift_names.m`, see the fixtures README): an
    Objective-C root class whose runtime name is the Swift form
    `_TtC4main7Greeter` (what swiftc emits for `@objc class Greeter` in
    module `main`), and an exported function under the Swift 5 symbol
    `_$s4main10countWords2ofS2i_tF` (`main.countWords(of: Swift.Int) ->
    Swift.Int`). The ObjC pass is on in both passes so the class name
    reaches the method label.

    Pass 1 (`option swiftdemangle off`) reproduces the BUG: the function is
    `$s4main10countWords2ofS2i_tF` and the method `-[_TtC4main7Greeter greet:]`.
    Pass 2 (`option swiftdemangle on`, the default) is the FIX: the same two
    functions are `main.countWords(of:)` and `-[main.Greeter greet:]`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
